WEBVTT

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.350
I've been waiting for you.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:43.940
Is she for sale?

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.810
She's my daughter.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.190
My apologies.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.530
But, Boss...

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:57.780
You know that this is no place to bring your daughter.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.660
She'll be running my gang someday.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.710
She needs to learn about everything.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.460
Then you'll be choosing one as well, Miss?

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.710
Choose one?

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:10.300
Yes...

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.840
I hope you find one you like.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:50.170
Oh? I didn't expect you to actually pick one.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.300
What is it, Kumiko?

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:57.010
You want him?

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.990
That dream again...

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:35.800
All the laughter, all the tears—everything happened just to meet you

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.460
Always go

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.880
On my own

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.100
Always go

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:54.730
The wind blows my overflowing tears away (the wind blows them away)

00:02:54.940 --> 00:03:02.070
I try to reach out my hand time after time toward what's to come

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:08.200
I've been hurt before by careless words

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:17.130
It's time I move forward with that unchangeable past

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.680
All the laughter, all the tears—

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:30.310
everything that has happened brought me to you

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:36.360
All we have left is the future

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:42.780
Please become our reason to continue living

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:49.500
And then the sun will once again shine on us

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.960
I've been trying everything to track down the Designer's Children,

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.880
but I still haven't been able to determine their whereabouts.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.130
I guess we'll have to rely on your power, after all.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.760
She says we'll have to rely on you.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:10.980
During the last battle, the Machine Goodfellow didn't activate.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.770
Teppei, you're still awake?

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:18.020
And yet, Amarok and Malkin appeared...

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:22.740
I think one of the two remaining
Designer's Children was nearby.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:26.780
Hana predicted a flow of Orgone energy,

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:29.200
but the Machine Goodfellow didn't activate.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.870
Does that mean there was something there, other than a Machine Goodfellow,

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:35.710
that also uses Orgone energy?

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:38.420
Something about it felt different from usual.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.880
Pitz is saying.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.720
That's interesting.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.340
What do you think, Captain?

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:47.550
The captain is sleeping.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.930
He really is sleeping.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.230
The captain's asleep?

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.610
Why not give him a goodnight kiss?

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:00.530
Is he really asleep?

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.280
Yeah, he's out cold.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.030
Would that be okay?

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.200
I guess so?

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.680
Goodnight, Captain.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:48.530
Is this really what the Japanese
independent attack force should be?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.620
The wait is over.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.580
Now for tonight's main event!

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.330
The challenger:

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:01.340
the last living carnivorous dinosaur in all of Asia...

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:03.670
Devil Zynus!

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.130
And...

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.800
How long will his win streak last?

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.470
The undefeated emperor,

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.970
the champion of this arena...

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:17.600
Baku!

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.040
That's it!

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.290
That's the match!

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:42.790
Fast! That was so fast!

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:45.880
The massive Devil Zynus fell in just ten seconds.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.760
Just ten seconds, and he's on the floor of the ring!

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:52.680
The giant impact of the champion's right fist

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:57.810
has slain the last living dinosaur!

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.810
Baku! Baku! Baku! Baku!

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:05.440
Baku! Baku! Baku! Baku! Baku! Baku!

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:05.440
Boys' Battlefield

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:17.620
Baku, you don't have to keep doing this.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.290
It's what your father ordered.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:23.040
You don't have to just do what he says.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.460
I'll talk to him!

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:26.590
It's fine.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:29.720
These fights are nothing.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:33.930
Please stop that.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.010
I'm all sweaty.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:38.060
And...

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:42.310
You have a fiancé, Miss.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.230
You have a nice smell.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.280
It's like the sun.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:53.990
Here.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.580
It's a mascot that's supposed to help you sleep at night.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.450
I have one too.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:04.460
Thank you.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.340
Do you think

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:12.550
they can really keep the nightmares away?

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.550
I hope so...

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.720
I guess it's a little childish, though.

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:22.600
Miss...

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.150
You were wonderful out there tonight, Baku!

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:28.980
Thanks to you, we always make loads of money every night.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:34.700
But the money you win, and <i>you</i>, are property of the Asanoda Yakuza.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.410
Never forget that.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.910
I'm told that your grades are good, too.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.790
Be grateful to the lady.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:45.000
She's the one who allows you to go to school.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:47.920
That's none of your business.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.460
Well, Miss, it's time to go home.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.590
I can go by myself. Leave me.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.550
I can't do that.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.300
Your father's orders.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:12.320
You guys are always eating something.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.490
It's important!

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:14.990
This is good.

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:17.410
I wonder if there's a pool around here.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:18.990
Want to go swimming again?

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:22.830
We shouldn't be playing around.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:25.080
It's important to pace yourself!

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.290
Pace yourself?

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:49.900
How nice.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:54.690
Hey, Captain...

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.240
Keep looking forward.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.910
Have you ever kissed anyone?

00:09:58.910 --> 00:09:59.950
What?

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.200
Is it important?

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.040
It's important.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.870
N-Not yet. Why?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:14.590
I see.

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:16.340
Roger, Captain.

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:19.970
Hey, what was that about?

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.350
They look so happy.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:33.690
But they're all dead if the Kill-T-Gangs reach Earth.

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:38.070
We won't let that happen. No matter what!

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:44.450
Yes? This is Manatsu.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:46.790
How is the town looking?

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:49.830
We haven't found anything yet.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:52.540
I uncovered something interesting.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:53.960
Sending the information now.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:58.420
There's an illegal underground arena in this city.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:01.550
An underground arena?

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:04.930
They hold unauthorized fighting tournaments,

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:08.480
and the audience bets on the winners.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.310
That sounds suspicious.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:13.610
I'll be sending agents from another team there tonight—

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.280
No, the Midsummer's Knights will go!

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:20.070
We should be handling stuff like that ourselves!

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:21.740
Right, Captain?

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.950
I guess so.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.780
All right!

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.370
By the way, Miss,

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:32.920
does it work?

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:34.840
What are you talking about?

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:40.130
That little charm you gave Baku last night.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:47.560
Is it true that it brings deep sleep without nightmares?

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.270
I'd love to have a mascot

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:54.770
that matches yours, too.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:56.900
Um, Sir...

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:02.740
Is there really a charm that can keep you from having nightmares?

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.990
If there is, I want one too.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:09.200
Idiot.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.830
Of course there's no such thing.

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:34.480
Excuse me. Do you have an invitation?

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:36.690
Will this do?

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:48.910
Minors are not permitted here.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.750
U-Um...

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.960
Will this suffice to change your mind?

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.080
We're here for "educational" purposes.

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:02.170
Go ahead. I hope you learn something.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:12.680
This has happened before, hasn't it?

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.460
The wait is over.

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:36.790
Now for tonight's main event!

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:39.170
Tonight's challenger:

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:42.460
The ultimate murder weapon of the Northern Hemisphere...

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.510
Gimerock Bomber!

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.390
And against him is the man you're all familiar with.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:55.930
The fighting prince of the arena...

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:57.940
the champion, Baku!

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:06.240
I've never seen you before.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.110
Who're you betting on?

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:11.160
What are the odds on the champion tonight?

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.740
1.2 to 1.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:15.540
All right... I'm in for 2,000,000 yen!

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.250
You have guts, little girl.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:20.330
Okay!

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:22.920
All right! Come on, champion!

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:27.300
Is this the real reason you wanted to come?

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:34.520
Whoa! He starts by pulling out a knife!

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:38.270
But any melee weapon is allowed.

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:42.110
The murder weapon's blade is slicing back and forth!

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:45.320
Will it find his prey?

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:46.240
Baku...

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:56.580
All right!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.000
That was amazing.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:03.290
No contest!

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:07.420
Once again, Baku's fists explode into his enemy!

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.760
The ultimate murder weapon of the Northern Hemisphere

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:12.680
was no match for the invincible champion.

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:19.020
Whoa! This is a surprise!

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:23.230
Our arena always welcomes surprise challengers,

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:27.190
but this is the first time we've actually had one!

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:30.990
So, tell us your name, hero!

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:34.990
I am... Amara.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:43.830
Amarok...

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:45.540
Teppei.

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:48.300
Not here.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.850
Ranged weapons are against the rules, huh?

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:57.890
Is that...

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:10.320
Our brave challenger's name is Amara!

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:15.160
Amara and the champion, Baku,
are staring each other down.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:18.370
The tension is immense...

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:44.100
What?

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:50.280
This brings back memories, Bagbear.

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:52.990
I remember when we used to play like this.

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:13.630
Who...

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:15.630
are you?

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:20.350
Stay away from me!

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:25.520
Whoa! Is this an earthquake?

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:31.820
Bagbear's heart is causing space itself to shake.

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:40.950
Turn on the emergency lights.

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:42.410
Hurry!

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.960
Baku, are you okay?

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:55.420
Amarok...

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:06.100
Who's there?

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.310
Come out.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:14.440
What? It isn't Bagbear?

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:17.030
Remember me, punk?

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.530
I don't think so...

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:20.950
Who are you?

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:23.990
I think his name was Kariya Haruhiko.

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:27.460
He was at the casino where I worked.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:30.960
Is that you, Zin?

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.170
So you were working with him.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:38.760
Those iron pipes leaning against
that wall over there...

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:40.340
They're dangerous.

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:45.220
You know you have to pay for what you did.

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:48.810
Didn't I just warn you about those pipes?

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:00.030
Sir! Sir!

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.490
You bastards...

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:28.230
Oh my, you aren't very friendly, mister.

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:34.520
A girl's standing here all alone, and you just walk by?

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:37.530
Are you with him?

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.570
"With him" isn't right.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:41.320
We're bound by fate.

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:44.570
Who are you people?

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:47.580
You could call us scouts.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:50.210
I don't like hitting women.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.000
Get lost.

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:54.670
Don't destroy who I am now.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:58.630
But that's exactly what we're here to do!

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:05.470
I thought you didn't hit women.

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:07.890
But ranged weapons are against the rules.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:09.600
Wait, Bagbear!

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:14.520
He's gone.

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:18.690
And I was going to show him a good time.

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:24.240
Sir... Sir... Sir!

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.700
His pupils are dilated.

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:29.870
He isn't breathing, and we can't find a pulse.

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:35.630
We'll have to wait for a doctor
to say for sure, but he's...

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:41.630
S-Sir...

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.090
No way!

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:48.220
His heart's stopped!

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:53.560
What's going on?

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:55.650
Are you really okay?

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:00.110
I'm immortal.

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:05.740
If Amarok and Malkin were there,
then a Designer's Child must have been there too.

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:08.370
Let's go back tomorrow.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:09.370
Yeah.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:11.580
This time without Akari.

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:13.580
Want my chips?

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:17.540
I knew something was wrong.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:19.670
What is it?

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:24.050
I looked into the Asanoda Yakuza while checking out the underground arena...

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:27.550
The Magus incident.

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:10.850
You're sweating an awful lot.

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:12.560
Did you have a bad dream?

00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:18.600
Hey, am I really the one you...

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:24.030
No, never mind.

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:42.040
Don't destroy who I am now.

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:55.060
The gentle breeze sweeps away even tears

00:22:55.060 --> 00:23:00.480
Even the recollections of the way of the stars

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:05.320
aren't always good things

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:12.990
I met you again on that faraway day

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:22.460
Even though we're as close as we are, this distant day is beginning

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:30.720
You can hear my voice calling out when I'm all alone

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:36.680
More than just love, it's hard to put into words

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:42.520
I'm searching for what to say while I walk beside you

00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:45.610
Instead of saying goodbye,

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:53.780
I'll just put these love spun tears in my right pocket again tomorrow

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:57.200
Love is spreading across the world

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:03.330
And I finally found it, by your side

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:14.970
We were right.

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:19.640
Baku, the boy from the arena, is a member of the Planetary Gears.

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:24.400
But Baku instinctively fears contact
with Amarok and the others.

00:24:25.360 --> 00:24:28.610
Will he pilot his Machine Goodfellow?

00:24:29.480 --> 00:24:32.990
Next time, on episode 13 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:34.990
My Town.

00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:34.990
My Town

00:24:34.990 --> 00:24:37.410
Earth Engine, scramble!
